state: implementation already landed in commit 9953ae5e3 (phase-38/10-inbound: persist all inbound /api/v1 requests to api_call_logs); only the log artifact was missing in the working tree, so this run reconstructs the gate evidence.
file:internal/api/api_call_log_middleware.go      present (581 lines): APICallLogger iface, asyncAPICallLogger w/ buffered ch (default 4096), worker goroutine batches up to 100 entries / 1s and calls APICallLogBatchInserter.CreateBatch; non-blocking Enqueue with select{default:} drop+counter; Shutdown closes channel and waits for done; redactURLAndHeaders helper masks Authorization/Cookie and any header/query name matching (?i)token|key|secret|password|cookie -> REDACTED; recursive JSON body redaction; cappedBuffer at 10KB with truncated marker; double recover (handler-panic + recorder-panic); SetAPICallLogger/GetAPICallLogger registry; DefaultAPILogSkip excludes /healthz /readyz /metrics /api/v1/admin/api-logs /api/v1/admin/api-logs/stats /api/v1/api-logs /api/v1/api-logs/stats /api/v1/events /api/v1/sse-token /api/v1/system/status.
file:internal/api/api_call_log_middleware_test.go present (816 lines): T01..T15 from the Prompt 09 test matrix.
file:internal/database/api_call_log_repo.go       CreateBatch via pgx.CopyFromSlice using same column order as Create; empty batch is no-op.
file:internal/config/config.go                    APILogsConfig with Enabled/CaptureBodies/QueueCapacity/BatchSize/FlushInterval; bound from API_LOGS_INBOUND_ENABLED (default true), API_LOG_CAPTURE_BODIES (default false), API_LOG_QUEUE_CAPACITY (4096), API_LOG_BATCH_SIZE (100), API_LOG_FLUSH_INTERVAL (1s).
file:internal/api/router.go                       inside r.Route("/api/v1", ...), r.Use(APICallLogMiddleware(GetAPICallLogger(), cfg.APILogs.CaptureBodies, DefaultAPILogSkip)) is registered BEFORE r.Use(ForwardAuthMiddleware(...)) so 401 responses are still captured.
file:cmd/teslasync/main.go                        constructs api.NewAsyncAPICallLogger(apiLogRepo, AsyncLoggerOptions{...}) when cfg.APILogs.Enabled, calls api.SetAPICallLogger, and on shutdown invokes inboundAPILogger.Shutdown(shutdownCtx).
file:docker-compose.yml                           five env vars present (API_LOGS_INBOUND_ENABLED, API_LOG_CAPTURE_BODIES, API_LOG_QUEUE_CAPACITY, API_LOG_BATCH_SIZE, API_LOG_FLUSH_INTERVAL).
file:helm/teslasync/templates/configmap.yaml      same five env vars rendered from .Values.config.apiLogs.* with safe defaults in the else branch.
file:helm/teslasync/values.yaml                   apiLogs sub-block under config: { inboundEnabled: true, captureBodies: false, queueCapacity: 4096, batchSize: 100, flushInterval: "1s" }.

